 [x] 1 Network  [x] 2 Protection  [>] 3 Admin  [ ] 4 Recovery  [ ] 5 Sign-in

 The first admin is an owner: they add other admins and approve elevated
 shells. Their name is their login: 2 to 31 lowercase letters, digits, _ or -,
 starting with a letter. root, maint, enrol, sshd, sshkeys, nobody, osadmin
 and console are taken.

 Next, their SSH key is enrolled: over SSH with a code shown here, or typed or
 fetched on this console.

 "root" can't be an admin name: use 2 to 31 lowercase letters, digits, _ or -,
 starting with a letter, and not a reserved name.


